From 24748a76f368b8f40f55d021f3853c0772fd5252 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:39:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(rfork): harden shutdown and planner errors

Guard RFork session shutdown against reentrant cleanup and unregister the atexit callback after successful finalization. Preserve retries when cleanup remains incomplete.

Limit planner exception handling to expected request, validation, and configuration failures so unexpected programming errors remain visible.

Document intentional transfer contracts: dense reshape and transpose handling, processed NZ logical-byte transfers, and checkpoint-only regenerated MLA/SFA tensors are deliberate RFork protocol choices rather than missing validation.

Signed-off-by: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
